#original-page(595.22pt, 842pt, (image("graphics/page-01.png", width: 229pt), 311pt, 156pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.036pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(67.32pt, 66.958pt, "RESIDUAL STRESS ANISOTROPY IN THIN-FILM LITHIUM NIOBATE ")
  #line-at(192pt, 83.038pt, "FOR STRESS-MANAGED MEMS ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.996pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(67.56pt, 96.958pt, "Byeongjin Kim, Ian Anderson, Tzu-Hsuan Hsu, Ziqian Yao, Mihir Chaudhari, Sinwoo Cho, and ")
  #line-at(267pt, 110.758pt, "Ruochen Lu, ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.996pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(204.84pt, 124.558pt, "The University of Texas at Austin, US ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.996pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 152.398pt, "ABSTRACT ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.957pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 164.159pt, "In this work, we present the first experimental study of ")
  #line-at(54pt, 175.679pt, "residual stress and post-release beam deflection in 128° Y-")
  #line-at(54pt, 187.199pt, "cut thin-film lithium niobate (TFLN) on Si, revealing ")
  #line-at(53.995pt, 198.719pt, "pronounced stress anisotropy with in-plane orientation. ")
  #line-at(54pt, 210.239pt, "Using optical profilometry with curvature fitting, we ")
  #line-at(54pt, 221.639pt, "extract gradient stress (σ₁) to build orientation-resolved ")
  #line-at(54pt, 233.159pt, "stress maps across multiple film thicknesses (100, 220, 460 ")
  #line-at(54pt, 244.679pt, "nm). For films in the 220–460 nm range, we identify stress-")
  #line-at(54pt, 256.199pt, "free in-plane orientations near ~55° and 125°, enabling ")
  #line-at(54pt, 267.719pt, "extremely flat suspended beams. In contrast, ultra-thin 100 ")
  #line-at(54pt, 279.239pt, "nm films exhibit shifted stress-free orientations near ~20° ")
  #line-at(54pt, 290.639pt, "and 160°. Leveraging these orientations, we demonstrate ")
  #line-at(54pt, 302.159pt, "extremely long suspended beams up to 2 cm in length, 10 ")
  #line-at(54pt, 313.679pt, "µm in width, and 460 nm in thickness without collapse. ")
  #line-at(54pt, 325.199pt, "These results establish in-plane stress anisotropy and ")
  #line-at(54pt, 336.719pt, "thickness selection in TFLN as a practical design lever for ")
  #line-at(54pt, 348.119pt, "mechanically ")
  #line-at(118.32pt, 348.119pt, "stable, ")
  #line-at(155.28pt, 348.119pt, "scalable, ")
  #line-at(201.24pt, 348.119pt, "and ")
  #line-at(226.8pt, 348.119pt, "stress-managed ")
  #line-at(54pt, 359.639pt, "microelectromechanical systems (MEMS). ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.996pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 386.999pt, "KEYWORDS")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.957pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 398.759pt, "Residual stress anisotropy, 128°Y-cut TFLN, stress ")
  #line-at(54pt, 410.279pt, "extraction, stress-managed MEMS. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.996pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 435.359pt, "INTRODUCTION")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.957pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 447.119pt, "Residual stress is a critical factor in determining the ")
  #line-at(54pt, 458.519pt, "reliability of thin-film MEMS, radio frequency (RF) ")
  #line-at(54pt, 470.039pt, "devices, and optical systems. Excessive residual stress can ")
  #line-at(54pt, 481.559pt, "cause devices to collapse, break, or degrade performance ")
  #line-at(54pt, 493.079pt, "during release (Fig. 1). Similar concerns have been widely ")
  #line-at(54pt, 504.599pt, "reported in thin-film systems, where tensile residual stress ")
  #line-at(54pt, 516.119pt, "can lead to film cracking [1]-[2]. Compressive residual ")
  #line-at(54pt, 527.519pt, "stress can cause peeling, buckling, or blistering of the layer ")
  #line-at(54pt, 539.039pt, "stack [3]-[4]. Residual-stress distributions are also known ")
  #line-at(54pt, 550.559pt, "to affect adhesion, fracture toughness of thin films [5], and ")
  #line-at(54pt, 562.079pt, "shift the resonant behavior of microelectromechanical and ")
  #line-at(54pt, 573.599pt, "nanoelectromechanical systems (MEMS and NEMS) [6]. ")
  #line-at(54pt, 584.999pt, "However, when properly controlled, stress can also be ")
  #line-at(54pt, 596.519pt, "exploited as a useful tuning mechanism. Engineered stress ")
  #line-at(54pt, 608.039pt, "has been shown to enhance electrical conductivity [7], ")
  #line-at(54pt, 619.559pt, "modify ")
  #line-at(95.16pt, 619.559pt, "the ")
  #line-at(119.76pt, 619.559pt, "dielectric ")
  #line-at(169.315pt, 619.559pt, "permittivity ")
  #line-at(228.96pt, 619.559pt, "[8], ")
  #line-at(255.6pt, 619.559pt, "increase ")
  #line-at(53.995pt, 631.079pt, "piezoelectricity [9], tailor magnetic anisotropy [10], and ")
  #line-at(54pt, 642.599pt, "even improve acoustic resonator performance [11]. These ")
  #line-at(54pt, 653.999pt, "examples highlight that residual stress is not merely a ")
  #line-at(53.995pt, 665.519pt, "byproduct of fabrication but a design parameter that can be ")
  #line-at(54pt, 677.039pt, "intentionally utilized to optimize device performance. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 688.559pt, "In lithium niobate (LN), the strong elastic anisotropy ")
  #line-at(54pt, 700.079pt, "and piezoelectric coupling make device performance ")
  #line-at(54pt, 711.599pt, "sensitive to residual stress and its in-plane distribution. ")
  #line-at(54pt, 722.999pt, "More recently, suspended devices built in transferred thin-")
  #line-at(54pt, 734.519pt, "film lithium niobate (TFLN) have been widely adopted for ")
  #line-at(54pt, 746.039pt, "RF resonators [12], filters [13], photonics [14], and ")
  #line-at(54pt, 757.559pt, "optomechanical applications [15].  ")
  #line-at(324.36pt, 512.399pt, "Residual stress in LN has been previously investigated ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 523.919pt, "in the context of bulk and thin-film acoustic devices. ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 535.439pt, "Thermal cycling in bulk SAW devices has been shown to ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 546.839pt, "induce significant residual stress that impacts reliability ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 558.359pt, "and crack formation [16]. Additionally, the influence of ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 569.879pt, "residual stress on acoustic wave propagation in ")
  #line-at(306.355pt, 581.399pt, "piezoelectric LN layers has been investigated, revealing ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 592.919pt, "changes in wave slowness and coupling behavior [17]. ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 604.439pt, "Residual stress has also been observed in epitaxial LN ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 615.839pt, "films, where substrate clamping influences out-of-plane ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 627.359pt, "thermal expansion and phase stability [18]. However, to ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 638.879pt, "date, no report has addressed the thickness-dependent and ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 650.399pt, "in-plane orientation-dependent residual stress distribution ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 661.919pt, "in transferred TFLN. The lack of systematic stress ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 673.439pt, "characterization limits scalability and yield. This is ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 684.839pt, "especially important recently, as acoustic devices in TFLN ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 696.359pt, "are now operating at higher frequencies, necessitating the ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 707.879pt, "study of thinner films [19]-[20], which are more ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 719.399pt, "susceptible to the impact of stress.  ")
  #line-at(324.36pt, 730.919pt, "In this work, we experimentally map the in-plane, ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 742.439pt, "thickness-dependent residual stress in 128° Y-cut TFLN ")
  #line-at(306.36pt, 753.839pt, "and identify stress-free orientations near 55° and 125° for ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.957pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(307.8pt, 286.919pt, "Fig. 1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.957pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(333.96pt, 286.919pt, ": Schematic and SEM/optical images of thin-film ")
  #line-at(307.795pt, 298.439pt, "piezoelectric MEMS illustrating stress-induced failure ")
  #line-at(307.8pt, 309.839pt, "modes: (a) membrane break due to stress gradient and (b) ")
  #line-at(307.795pt, 321.359pt, "post-release membrane collapsing.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.957pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(307.8pt, 434.039pt, "Fig. 2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.957pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(337.2pt, 434.039pt, ": (a) Decomposition of residual stress in a ")
  #line-at(307.8pt, 445.559pt, "micromachined TFLN cantilever into mean σ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.478pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(513.36pt, 446.519pt, "0")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.957pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(516.6pt, 445.559pt, " and ")
  #line-at(307.795pt, 457.079pt, "gradient stress σ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.478pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(377.28pt, 458.039pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.957pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(380.52pt, 457.079pt, ". (b) Four FEA-predicted post-release ")
  #line-at(307.8pt, 468.599pt, "beam shapes produced by these stresses; colors denote ")
  #line-at(307.8pt, 479.999pt, "displacement. ")
